{"id": "9th-u7-q080", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "matching", "level": "analysis", "difficulty": "hard", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "9th-tamil-u7", "lesson_id": "9th-tamil-u7-l2", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "sivaka-chinthamani-matching", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "பொருத்துக (சீவக சிந்தாமணிச் சொற்கள் - பொருள்கள்):\n(a) தெங்கு - 1. உச்சி\n(b) வருக்கை - 2. பாய்ந்து\n(c) நெற்றி - 3. தேங்காய்\n(d) மடுத்து - 4. பலாப்பழம்", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "(a)-4, (b)-3, (c)-2, (d)-1", "B": "(a)-1, (b)-2, (c)-4, (d)-3", "C": "(a)-2, (b)-1, (c)-3, (d)-4", "D": "(a)-3, (b)-4, (c)-1, (d)-2"}, "explanation": "தெங்கு = தேங்காய் (3); வருக்கை = பலாப்பழம் (4); நெற்றி = உச்சி (1); மடுத்து = பாய்ந்து (2). சரியான வரிசை: 3, 4, 1, 2."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Match the classical vocabulary terms from Sivaka Chinthamani with their meanings:\n(a) Thengu - 1. Summit / Crown\n(b) Varukkai - 2. Flowing forth\n(c) Netri - 3. Coconut\n(d) Madhuthu - 4. Jackfruit", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "(a)-4, (b)-3, (c)-2, (d)-1", "B": "(a)-1, (b)-2, (c)-4, (d)-3", "C": "(a)-2, (b)-1, (c)-3, (d)-4", "D": "(a)-3, (b)-4, (c)-1, (d)-2"}, "explanation": "Thengu -> Coconut (3); Varukkai -> Jackfruit (4); Netri -> Summit (1); Madhuthu -> Flowing forth (2). Sequence: 3, 4, 1, 2."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "D", "accepted_keys": ["D"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 134, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 134", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["9th_tamil", "iyal_7", "sivaka_chinthamani", "vocabulary_matching"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u7-q081", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "factual", "level": "medium", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "9th-tamil-u7", "lesson_id": "9th-tamil-u7-l2", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "sivaka-chinthamani-five-fruits", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "சீவக சிந்தாமணியின் முதற்பாடலில் தேங்காய் விழும் வேகத்தில் அடுத்தடுத்துத் தாக்கப்படும் கனிகள்/மரங்கள் எவை?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "பாக்கு மரத்துத் தேன்கூடு, பலாப்பழம், மாங்கனி, வாழைப்பழம்", "B": "கொய்யா, மாதுளை, திராட்சை, அத்தி", "C": "நெல்லி, நாவல், எலுமிச்சை, விளாம்பழம்", "D": "ஆப்பிள், ஆரஞ்சு, பப்பாளி, முந்திரி"}, "explanation": "உயர்ந்த தென்னையிலிருந்து விழும் தேங்காய் பாக்கின் உச்சித் தேனடையைக் கிழித்து, பலாப்பழத்தைப் பிளந்து, மாங்கனியைச் சிதறவைத்து, வாழைப்பழங்களை உதிர்த்தது என ஐந்து மர வளங்கள் பாடலில் வருகின்றன."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "In the opening verse of Namagal Ilambagam, what succession of fruits and trees are impacted by the falling coconut?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Areca honeycomb, jackfruit, mango, and bananas (பாக்கு, பலா, மா, வாழை)", "B": "Guava, pomegranate, grapes, and fig", "C": "Gooseberry, jamun, lemon, and wood-apple", "D": "Apple, orange, papaya, and cashew"}, "explanation": "The falling coconut pierces the honeycomb atop the areca tree, cleaves the jackfruit, shatters mangoes, and dislodges bananas."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "A", "accepted_keys": ["A"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, 