{"id": "9th-u7-q113", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "factual", "level": "easy", "difficulty": "easy", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "9th-tamil-u7", "lesson_id": "9th-tamil-u7-l4", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "aagupeyar-definition", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "ஒன்றன் இயற்பெயர், அதனோடு தொடர்புடைய மற்றொன்றிற்குத் தொன்றுதொட்டு ஆகிவருவது எவ்வாறு அழைக்கப்படும்?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "ஆகுபெயர்", "B": "அன்மொழித்தொகை", "C": "இடைச்சொல்", "D": "உரிச்சொல்"}, "explanation": "ஒன்றன் இயற்பெயர், தனக்குரிய பொருளைக் குறிக்காமல் அதனோடு தொடர்புடைய மற்றொன்றிற்கு ஆகிவருவது 'ஆகுபெயர்' (Metonymy) எனப்படும்."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "What grammatical phenomenon describes an innate name transferring its primary semantic designation to an associated object?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Aagupeyar (ஆகுபெயர் - Metonymy / Transferred naming)", "B": "Anmozhithogai", "C": "Idaichol", "D": "Urichol"}, "explanation": "When a primary noun shifts its reference to another entity closely linked to it, it is termed Aagupeyar."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "A", "accepted_keys": ["A"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 65, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Pa